Package: grist
Title: Mergeable Sufficient Statistics on S2 Cells from Daily Grids
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: person("Michael", "Sumner", email = "mdsumner@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: The engine extracted from trend.sst: area-weighted daily
    grids accumulated to a global S2 discrete grid as sufficient
    statistics (count, summed weights, weighted sums and sums of
    squares), one Parquet file per date. A source is a catalog of
    (date, dsn, band) plus a grid signature; a region is a cell
    selection; every mean, variance, or rollup is exact arithmetic on
    the sums. Deployments (product knowledge, catalogs, schedules,
    sites) live in host repositories; this package is the invariant
    middle.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports: s2, vapour, vaster, arrow, dplyr
Suggests: mirai, jsonlite
URL: https://github.com/hypertidy/grist
BugReports: https://github.com/hypertidy/grist/issues
